  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing (NAICS 336412) has $5B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The sector recorded 8,012 awards with an average award size of $622K. Obligations are down 58.5% year over year. The Department of Defense led buying with $4.9B in obligations, making it by far the largest federal customer in this NAICS. FY2026 to date totals sit below recent peaks: FY23 reached $13.7B and FY25 reached $12B. The vendor list is concentrated at the top: RTX CORPORATION received $1.6B, GENERAL ELECTRIC COMPANY received $1.2B and ROLLS-ROYCE CORPORATION received $723M in FY2026 to date. Smaller federal buyers include the Department of Homeland Security with $74M and several civilian agencies with single-digit million or lower totals. The FY2026 to date snapshot is partial and reflects obligations posted so far in the fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did FY2026 to date compare with recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Obligations for NAICS 336412 in FY2026 to date are $5B, which is lower than FY25 at $12B and FY23 at $13.7B. FY22 was $11.1B and FY21 was $7.3B. The FY2026 to date figure follows FY24 at $8.4B."
      },
